RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfKGen, in the twist reprocessing of a fillet stripe, reads the 3D line of the
neighbouring SurfData (DStr.Curve(previntf.LineIndex()).Curve() and the same for the next one) and calls D1 on it
without checking it. Fail the stripe with Standard_Failure (status ChFiDS_TwistedSurface, as the other failures of
this block do) when either line is missing, instead of dereferencing a null handle.

Why: ChFi3d_Purge (same file, called from PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine) collapses a SurfData at the end of a stripe onto
a vertex: it sets IndexOfS<n> to 0 and the interference's line index to 0, and keeps the SurfData in the stripe.
When the SurfData next to it was flagged twisted by the walking, the reprocessing compares face indices
(samesurfon is false because the purged neighbour has index 0), takes the "3D tangents of neighbours" branch and
asks the data structure for curve 0. TopOpeBRepDS_DataStructure::Curve returns its empty curve for an index that
is not bound (curves are numbered from 1), so the handle is null and D1 is called through it. Seen in RayCAD's
naming random test (sequence 18:37, a size-search trial fillet of 0.156 mm on a valid body): an access violation
on Windows, SIGSEGV on Linux. ChFi3d_Builder::Compute catches Standard_Failure per stripe and reports the contour
as failed, so callers see an ordinary fillet failure. Nothing else changes: the guard only fires where the code
would otherwise have dereferenced null.

Upstream: not fixed in OCCT master as of 2026-11-18 (no check on these handles; the later ChFi3d crash fixes, #1407
in StartSol and #1620, do not touch this code). Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -3545,6 +3545,13 @@
           // here the base is on 3D tangents of neighbors.
           const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& c3dprev1 = DStr.Curve(previntf1.LineIndex()).Curve();
           const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& c3dnext1 = DStr.Curve(nextintf1.LineIndex()).Curve();
+          if (c3dprev1.IsNull() || c3dnext1.IsNull())
+          {
+            // A neighbour without a 3D line (ChFi3d_Purge collapses an end SurfData onto a
+            // vertex and sets its line index to 0): fail the stripe instead of dereferencing null.
+            Spine->SetErrorStatus(ChFiDS_TwistedSurface);
+            throw Standard_Failure("adjustment by reprocessing the non-written points: no 3D curve");
+          }
           gp_Pnt                         Pdeb1, Pfin1;
           gp_Vec                         Vdeb1, Vfin1;
           c3dprev1->D1(prevpar1, Pdeb1, Vdeb1);
@@ -3616,6 +3623,13 @@
           // here the base is on 3D tangents of neighbors.
           const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& c3dprev2 = DStr.Curve(previntf2.LineIndex()).Curve();
           const occ::handle<Geom_Curve>& c3dnext2 = DStr.Curve(nextintf2.LineIndex()).Curve();
+          if (c3dprev2.IsNull() || c3dnext2.IsNull())
+          {
+            // A neighbour without a 3D line (ChFi3d_Purge collapses an end SurfData onto a
+            // vertex and sets its line index to 0): fail the stripe instead of dereferencing null.
+            Spine->SetErrorStatus(ChFiDS_TwistedSurface);
+            throw Standard_Failure("adjustment by reprocessing the non-written points: no 3D curve");
+          }
           gp_Pnt                         Pdeb2, Pfin2;
           gp_Vec                         Vdeb2, Vfin2;
           c3dprev2->D1(prevpar2, Pdeb2, Vdeb2);
